  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">How can I read if there are no books? (Indonesia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Half of Indonesian classrooms have no reading books available apart from textbooks. Without great reading books, children will not learn to read well.  For more than ten years, our team has built working relationships with local governments, schools and charities, all of whom are desperate for good quality reading books.  This project will provide a &quot;library in a box&quot; to at least five schools in every one of Indonesia&apos;s 34 provinces (170 schools in total).</narrative>
  </description>
